7. Deployment Scenarios

(Based on Test Documentation)

Scenario 1 — Initial Deployment

Developer creates new SQL objects.

Expected Behavior:

All SQL files detected

Executed sequentially

Metadata initialized

Validation:

Objects created

Metadata updated

Scenario 2 — Feature Branch Deployment

Developer modifies subset of SQL files.

Expected:

Only modified SQL deployed

No unrelated objects executed

Dev metadata updated

Scenario 3 — Merge to Main

After PR merge:

Expected:

Main contains feature changes

Non-prod deploy runs delta changes

Execution order preserved

Scenario 4 — Re-Deployment Without Changes

Expected:

No SQL execution

System reports No Changes Detected

Metadata unchanged

Scenario 5 — Production Promotion

System compares:

Non-prod metadata vs Prod metadata


Expected:

Only approved SQL promoted

Exact commit consistency maintained

Scenario 6 — Multiple Developer Changes

Developer A + Developer B commits.

Expected:

Combined delta detected

Ordered execution

Single deployment history entry

Scenario 7 — Rollback

Rollback job:

Reads previous deployment metadata

Reverts affected SQL objects

Restores previous state

